        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Polls show CDU ahead of Greens, boosting probability of CDU finishing with the most seats in at least some frames."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Greens current seat lead in the Landtag (154-seat baseline)",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Greens hold a higher seat count under the larger frame, challenging CDU's likelihood of claiming the most seats."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Late-February polls showing Greens narrowing the gap",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "New polls reducing CDU's edge add downside risk to CDU winning the most seats."
      },
      {
        "factor": "AfD vote share around 20% in polls",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Anti-establishment votes could siphon support from CDU and Greens, reducing the majorities and altering seat outcomes."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Turnout and regional variation uncertainty",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Turnout swings can materially affect seat allocations; uncertainty adds calibration noise."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Frame-size interpretation differences (120 vs 154 seats)",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Different frames produce conflicting implications for seat counts, complicating direct translation from polls to seats."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "The final probability is a synthesis across frames, giving more weight to the larger-frame Greens baseline and late-poll momentum in the updates, but not discarding CDU polling strength in some frames. The resulting probability of CDU achieving the most seats ends up around 0.50, with a calibrated range reflecting cross-frame uncertainty and potential tail risks."
  }
}
